2. Serial bridge tuning

Option A: Command-line override (quickest)


ros2 run pca9685_multiple servo_serial_bridge \
  --ros-args \
  -p port:=/dev/ttyACM0 \
  -p max_write_hz:=10 \
  -p min_change_rad:=0.02
max_write_hz:=10 → each joint gets a new serial command at most 10 times/second (100 ms between writes). Default was 20 Hz.
min_change_rad:=0.02 → only re-send if the joint moved more than ~1.1°. Default was 0.01 rad (~0.57°).
Option B: Launch file argument (if you add it to the launch)

Edit /home/ikbal/ros2_ws/src/mearm_bringup/launch/bringup.launch.py and add parameters to the servo_serial_bridge_node:


servo_serial_bridge_node = Node(
    package="pca9685_multiple",
    executable="servo_serial_bridge",
    name="servo_serial_bridge",
    output="screen",
    parameters=[
        {"port": LaunchConfiguration("serial_port")},
        {"baud": LaunchConfiguration("baud_rate")},
        {"max_write_hz": 10.0},
        {"min_change_rad": 0.02},
    ],
    condition=UnlessCondition(LaunchConfiguration("use_mock_hardware")),
)
Then rebuild (colcon build --packages-select mearm_bringup pca9685_multiple) and relaunch.

